All right.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:47.560
Episode 12 
The Rebels Set Sail

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:46.180
The ship will be leaving Colony Minsry in 10 minutes!

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:47.560
All hands to your stations!

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:51.270
What happened?

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.940
The Federation Forces entered the colony!

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:57.110
They wanted to arrest the captain for treason!{as a rebel, maybe "for treason"}

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.320
Flit, is it true?

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.120
The Federation Forces came after the captain?

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.160
Yes.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.040
We need to get away from this colony as soon as we can.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.040
Hurry and prepare for launch, Vargas!

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.040
O-Okay. Leave it to me!

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:14.710
Emily and Dique, too!

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:15.210
Right.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:16.460
Got it!

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:18.630
Where are you going, Flit?

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:22.300
Mr. Grodek told me to change into my pilot suit!

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.260
What's wrong?

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:28.140
We disobeyed the orders of the Federation Forces.{to oppose; to resist; to defy; smething else here}

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.310
Isn't it a bit late for that?

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.810
Sure, I hate the UE!

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:37.280
But to make an enemy of the Federation Forces as well...?{But having to fight the Federation Forces too...}{making the Federation forces into our enemy..}

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:40.450
Then you should get off this ship now.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.570
Woolf...

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:46.490
Largan, don't lose sight of what's important.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:51.290
In a race, sometimes you've gotta run an unfavorable course.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:56.460
But it's all so you can win in the end.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.720
About to switch from colony navigation to outer space navigation.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:12.980
Enemy detection systems have located what appear to be warships!

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:16.020
This is... IFF codes received!

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:19.150
They're Federation Forces Darwin-class space warships.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.780
Blitz, Haloes and Warden.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:28.780
You didn't really believe that it was over already, Grodek Ainoa?{Did you think you'd get off that easy, Grodek Ainoa?}

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:33.500
I won't let you off that easily{go just like that}... rebels!

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.760
A Federation fleet...

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:45.970
Are they here to arrest us?

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:48.300
Wh-What's going to happen to us?

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:51.600
Captain...

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:55.980
Advance at slow speed.

00:04:56.850 --> 00:05:02.900
The easiest way to capture us would have been seizing the ship before it launched.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:06.820
Then the Diva wouldn't have been able to escape.{Then the Diva would have had nowhere to run.}

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:12.410
Since they didn't do that, they're sending us a message.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:13.500
"Come on out."

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.550
That's right.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:22.380
That's just the way I like it.{That's the way (uh huh, uh huh) I like it, uh huh, uh huh}

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.670
I won't let any of you get away.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:29.100
I'll surround you and turn that ship itself into a prison.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:31.760
I'm surprised that they're coming out to us so readily.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.930
They must be confident.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:40.650
Grodek is a talented computer engineer, but that's not all.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:47.660
He was made deputy commander of Arinston Base due to his skill as a mission planner{male Sumeragi Lee Noriega?}.

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:51.120
He even got the better of you inside the colony, I suppose.

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:52.540
Don't be stupid.

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:56.540
Playing military policeman like that isn't my style.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:06:00.500
And of course, the appearance of the Gundam was an unexpected variable.{I didn't expect the Gundam.}

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:06.170
As a ship-going man, this kind of situation is more exciting.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.430
I'm glad to hear that, captain.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.550
But please take care not to eat too much.

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:11.550
Get off it!{Leave me alone!}

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:13.260
My brain's running at full speed.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:15.060
It wants chocolate!

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:21.940
Now then, what's your move, Grodek Ainoa?

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.820
Notify the mobile suit team.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.530
Prepare to launch.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:34.200
Yes, sir!

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:37.660
<i>All mobile suits, prepare to launch!</i>

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:41.040
<i>I say again, all mobile suits prepare to launch!</i>

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.040
Do we really have no choice?

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.790
We're all part of the Federation Forces!

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:00.900
Looks like they're sending out mobile suits.

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:04.020
Maybe Grodek is planning something.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:04.820
What do we do?

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:08.610
We have no obligation to let him make his move.

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:09.240
Are we ready?

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.400
Yes.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:13.820
Okay then, let the fireworks of battle begin!{of battle}

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:20.830
What?

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:27.340
Signal flares?

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:29.260
No, this is...

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:31.680
What's this light?

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:53.110
Flash rounds to temporarily blind them.

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:56.700
An old-fashioned strategy, but it's effective, isn't it?

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:58.990
Open a line to the Diva.

00:07:58.990 --> 00:07:59.540
Yes, sir.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.330
Channel open.

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:04.080
I am Commander Stoller Guavaran.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:09.460
I'm in charge of the EFF's 8th Space Fleet, Special Detachment.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:12.880
You are completely surrounded.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:17.050
Disengage your weapons at once and surrender peacefully.

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:24.150
Otherwise, you will be considered an enemy force, and we will attack with our full strength.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:27.570
What's the point in saying all that when you already have your guns pointed at us?{It's a bit late for that. They already have their guns pointed at us.}

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.570
Wait a moment, please!

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.450
Who are you?

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:37.870
I am the Diva's navigator, Ensign Adams Tinel.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:41.160
We have no intention of fighting the Federation Forces.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:42.580
Oh?

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:46.080
Captain Grodek has performed an independent investigation

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:50.760
and determined the UE are hiding in the abandoned space fortress Ambat.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:51.840
Adams...

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:56.140
We believe that this is the hour to strike the UE.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:57.680
If this operation is successful,

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:01.600
we will definitely deal a major blow to the UE.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:03.770
So please, Commander Guavaran,

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:05.940
if the 8th Space Fleet would just join forces with us...

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:07.060
I see.

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:09.360
An interesting story.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:15.360
But that's for the higher-ups to decide and no justification for you to act on your own.

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:18.410
If you're a soldier, you should understand that.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:24.460
My mission is simply to capture Grodek Ainoa.

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:28.420
Now, would you give me your answer, Grodek?

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:38.140
No answer?

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:40.260
You leave me no choice.{Very well.}

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:43.560
It's not my preference, but we'll have to do this by force.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:08.920
What?

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:11.590
What happened?

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:17.930
You too!

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:24.270
Well done, Flit!

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:33.440
Not bad.

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:39.530
They hid the Gundam in the colony's shadow, our detection system's blind spot.

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:40.360
Damage report?

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:44.790
Aside from the destruction of the beam spray guns, all three Genoaces are unharmed.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.290
Well, aren't they nice?{earnest/honest/kind/frank}

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:51.420
Mr. Grodek, let's take this chance to escape!

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:53.540
No, that's probably impossible.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:59.470
It looks like we've been targeted by the fleet's weapons control systems

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:02.890
as well as by the mobile suits deployed around us!

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:09.350
When did they launch their mobile suits?

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:10.730
When they fired the flash rounds.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:15.940
Then they used a few mobile suits to restrain the Diva,

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:21.660
and deployed the other suits while we were distracted.

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:23.320
B-But that means...

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:27.240
We completely fell for their plan.

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:32.500
Now what will you do, Grodek?

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:54.230
Will they surrender quietly?

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:55.650
I don't know.

00:11:55.650 --> 00:12:03.530
But even if they do resist and take out one of our ships, our other two will {definitely destroy}make short work of the Diva.

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:06.330
So they'll end up the same either way.

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:10.370
But now we're even.

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:18.050
What?

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:29.100
They were hiding a fleet!?

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:30.310
Calm down.

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:32.730
The firing will stop in a moment.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:40.860
Why?

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:43.200
Why must we cease fire?

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:47.910
You didn't take pity on them because you're all Federation Forces, did you?

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:49.030
That's not it.

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:52.870
We'll be moving on to Operation Ambat Capture from here. {catpure Ambat campaign}

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:56.500
I want to minimize loss of ammunition and damage to our ships.

00:12:56.500 --> 00:13:00.590
That's probably what Grodek's thinking.

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:04.050
He has a goal, and he doesn't want to waste resources on anything else.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:04.930
I see.

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:10.180
But if he managed to gather this many warships, he may be serious about attacking the UE...

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:13.350
But we have a job to do, too.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:19.480
Now what will you do?

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:27.610
What!?

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:29.700
Attack from behind the fleet!

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:30.530
Details unknown!

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:33.080
Do they have even more warships!?

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:34.370
No, they don't.

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:36.460
The detection systems aren't picking anything up.

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:38.540
This signature...

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:43.710
It's the UE!

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:02.980
Detection systems have acquired targets!

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:05.190
Two warships, ten mobile suit-types!

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:08.200
The Haloes mobile suit squad has suffered multiple casualties!

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:09.700
They can't hold the line!

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:13.410
Have our forward-line{front-deployed} mobile suits form a screen!

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:15.500
Make protecting the fleet our top priority!{Our highest priority is to protect the ship!}

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:16.000
Yes, sir!

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:19.120
This is a problem.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:23.960
If we keep our weapons aimed at the Diva, the UE will attack from behind.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:28.510
But if we turn around, we'll be exposing our back to the Diva...

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:33.140
We're in a tight spot for sure.

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:37.060
The 8th Space Fleet has engaged the UE!

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:38.600
Wh-What should we do?

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:39.900
Don't ask me.

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:44.440
This is an unexpected blessing.

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:50.610
Let the Federation Forces deal with the UE, and we'll leave this sector{airspace? plz. sector} and head for Ambat.

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:51.700
Impossible!

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.620
You want us to abandon our comrades!?

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:54.580
No.

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:56.200
They aren't comrades at all.

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:57.870
They're the enemy.

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.870
Remember what the captain said?

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:04.380
We should avoid loss of ammunition and damage to our ships.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:07.170
This is a once-in-a-lifetime chance.

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:07.800
But...

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:12.510
Or will you help your enemy, and be arrested as rebels?

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:17.720
Prepare to fire main guns!

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:19.890
Launch the mobile suits!

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:21.600
Attack the UE in front of us!

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:22.900
Yes, sir!

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:25.400
Sounds good to me!

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:30.950
In that case, I can go all out!

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:31.700
Captain!

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:32.360
What?

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:34.490
It's the Diva's mobile suits!

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:41.750
They're...

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:55.010
Get back. I'll handle this!

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:56.430
O-Okay...

00:15:57.720 --> 00:16:00.140
Come on! Come at me, bro!{change to "come at me, bro!"}{usrs?}

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:04.560
This'll be the perfect warm-up for Ambat!

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:13.530
I can... I can fight too!

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:31.220
We're...

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:34.800
We're...

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:37.470
We're going to Ambat to destroy the UE!

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:42.640
We're not going down here!{so derpy}

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:19.050
Why was I able to do that?

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:21.850
It was like I could predict the enemies' movements...

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:23.930
Stay sharp, Flit!

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:27.060
This fight isn't over yet!

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:27.400
Right!

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:32.280
The Diva's pilots aren't half bad.

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.700
Captain, the Diva is approaching at high speed!

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:38.280
Thermal sensors confirm they're charging their main guns!

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:44.120
You don't think they're planning to take us out with them, do you?

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:45.500
No, they're not.

00:17:56.880 --> 00:18:00.100
Evade the Diva's line of fire at full speed!

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:02.470
Clear a path for them!

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:15.240
Fire!

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:29.620
Jeez... They used our ship to hide from the enemy...

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:31.920
Open a channel to the Haloes and Warden!

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:33.460
This is your fleet commander.

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:35.880
All ships, hard to port!

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:38.970
Confirm firing system linkage!

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:41.800
Change target to the UE fleet!

